description:
Parse the line WinDbg prints when the VM stops on a bug check (lesson 1.05), and explain the common ones:

```cpp
struct BugCheck { std::uint32_t code; std::uint64_t p[4]; };

bool parseBugCheck(const std::string& line, BugCheck& out);
std::string bugCheckName(std::uint32_t code);
std::string explain(const BugCheck& b);
```

The line looks like `*** Fatal System Error: 0x000000d1 (0xFFFFA00012345678,0x0000000000000002,0x0000000000000000,0xFFFFF80123456789)`, possibly with spaces after the commas; the code and parameters are hexadecimal with `0x`, in either case. Anything that does not have exactly this shape (with four parameters) fails.

Names: `0x0A` IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL, `0x3B` SYSTEM_SERVICE_EXCEPTION, `0x50` PAGE_FAULT_IN_NONPAGED_AREA, `0x7E` SYSTEM_THREAD_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED, `0xC4` DRIVER_VERIFIER_DETECTED_VIOLATION, `0xCE` DRIVER_UNLOADED_WITHOUT_CANCELLING_PENDING_OPERATIONS, `0xD1` DRIVER_IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL; others `UNKNOWN_BUG_CHECK`.

`explain`:
- `0xD1` and `0x0A`: `"<read|write|execute> of 0x<p0> at IRQL <p1>"` where p2 is 0 read, 1 write, 8 execute (anything else `access`), and p0 is printed as 16 upper-case hex digits;
- `0x50`: `"<read|write> of invalid address 0x<p0>"` with p1 0 for read, anything else write;
- others: the name.

